{"entry":{"id":"l-ad3be2b27679026b","lemma":"أَبٌ","root":"ابو","arabic":"أَبَاهُمْ","gloss":"(to) their father","transliteration":"abāhum","representativeKey":"12:16:2","exampleKeys":["12:16:2","111:1:3","12:61:4"],"occurrenceCount":46,"courseOrder":232,"sourceIds":["qul-56","qul-92","qul-71","qul-75","qul-76","qul-301"],"rootId":"r-7ca0ea5bd6961515","approval":{"status":"pending"}},"examples":[{"ref":"12:16","tokens":[{"key":"12:16:1","position":1,"arabic":"وَجَآءُوٓ","kind":"word","gloss":"And they came","transliteration":"wajāū","lemma":"جَآءَ","root":"جيا","entryId":"l-1abf61bfcb8fdd4c"},{"key":"12:16:2","position":2,"arabic":"أَبَاهُمْ","kind":"word","gloss":"(to) their father","transliteration":"abāhum","lemma":"أَبٌ","root":"ابو","entryId":"l-ad3be2b27679026b"},{"key":"12:16:3","position":3,"arabic":"عِشَآءًۭ","kind":"word","gloss":"early at night","transliteration":"ʿishāan","lemma":"عِشَآء","root":"عشو","entryId":null},{"key":"12:16:4","position":4,"arabic":"يَبْكُونَ","kind":"word","gloss":"weeping","transliteration":"yabkūna","lemma":"بَكَتْ","root":"بكي","entryId":null},{"key":"12:16:5","position":5,"arabic":"١٦","kind":"end-marker","gloss":"","transliteration":"","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null}],"translation":"And they came to their father in the early part of the night weeping.","translationSource":"qul-301-hilali-khan","notes":[],"targetKey":"12:16:2","targetGloss":"(to) their father","targetTransliteration":"abāhum","sourceIds":["qul-56","qul-92","qul-71","qul-75","qul-76","qul-301"]},{"ref":"111:1","tokens":[{"key":"111:1:1","position":1,"arabic":"تَبَّتْ","kind":"word","gloss":"Perish","transliteration":"tabbat","lemma":"تَبَّ","root":"تبب","entryId":null},{"key":"111:1:2","position":2,"arabic":"يَدَآ","kind":"word","gloss":"(the) hands","transliteration":"yadā","lemma":"يَد","root":"يدي","entryId":"l-d6185269501ba306"},{"key":"111:1:3","position":3,"arabic":"أَبِى","kind":"word","gloss":"(of) Abu","transliteration":"abī","lemma":"أَبٌ","root":"ابو","entryId":"l-ad3be2b27679026b"},{"key":"111:1:4","position":4,"arabic":"لَهَبٍۢ","kind":"word","gloss":"Lahab","transliteration":"lahabin","lemma":"لَهَب","root":"لهب","entryId":null},{"key":"111:1:5","position":5,"arabic":"وَتَبَّ","kind":"word","gloss":"and perish he","transliteration":"watabba","lemma":"تَبَّ","root":"تبب","entryId":null},{"key":"111:1:6","position":6,"arabic":"١","kind":"end-marker","gloss":"","transliteration":"","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null}],"translation":"Perish the two hands of Abû Lahab (an uncle of the Prophet) and perish he!","translationSource":"qul-301-hilali-khan","notes":[{"text":"Narrated Ibn ‘Abbâs رضي الله عنهما : \"When the Verse, ‘And warn your tribe (O Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم) of near kindred.’ (V.26:214) was revealed, Allâh’s Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم went out, and when he had ascended As-Safâ mountain, he shouted, ‘Yâ Sabâhâh !’* The people said, ‘What is that?’ Then they gathered around him, whereupon he said, ‘Do you see? If I inform you that cavalrymen are proceeding up the side of this mountain, will you believe me?’ They said, ‘We have never heard you telling a lie.’ Then he said, ‘I am a plain warner to you of a coming severe punishment.’ Abû Lahab said, ‘May you perish! You gathered us only for this reason?’ Then Abu Lahab went away. So [Sûrat Al-Masad] ‘Perish the hands of Abu Lahab!’ was revealed. (V.111:1). (Sahih Al-Bukhari, Vol. 6, Hadith No.495). * \"Yâ Sabâhâh!\" is an Arabic expression used when one appeals for help or draws the attention of others to some danger.","ref":null}],"targetKey":"111:1:3","targetGloss":"(of) Abu","targetTransliteration":"abī","sourceIds":["qul-56","qul-92","qul-71","qul-75","qul-76","qul-301"]},{"ref":"12:61","tokens":[{"key":"12:61:1","position":1,"arabic":"قَالُوا۟","kind":"word","gloss":"They said","transliteration":"qālū","lemma":"قَالَ","root":"قول","entryId":"l-effaf24a5c86c56f"},{"key":"12:61:2","position":2,"arabic":"سَنُرَٰوِدُ","kind":"word","gloss":"We will try to get permission","transliteration":"sanurāwidu","lemma":"رَٰوَدُ","root":"رود","entryId":null},{"key":"12:61:3","position":3,"arabic":"عَنْهُ","kind":"word","gloss":"for him","transliteration":"ʿanhu","lemma":"عَن","root":null,"entryId":"l-f1109a78c8548754"},{"key":"12:61:4","position":4,"arabic":"أَبَاهُ","kind":"word","gloss":"(from) his father","transliteration":"abāhu","lemma":"أَبٌ","root":"ابو","entryId":"l-ad3be2b27679026b"},{"key":"12:61:5","position":5,"arabic":"وَإِنَّا","kind":"word","gloss":"and indeed we","transliteration":"wa-innā","lemma":"إِنّ","root":null,"entryId":"l-3afba549abbd5639"},{"key":"12:61:6","position":6,"arabic":"لَفَـٰعِلُونَ","kind":"word","gloss":"surely will do","transliteration":"lafāʿilūna","lemma":"فَاعِل","root":"فعل","entryId":null},{"key":"12:61:7","position":7,"arabic":"٦١","kind":"end-marker","gloss":"","transliteration":"","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null}],"translation":"They said: \"We shall try to get permission (for him) from his father, and verily, we shall do it.\"","translationSource":"qul-301-hilali-khan","notes":[],"targetKey":"12:61:4","targetGloss":"(from) his father","targetTransliteration":"abāhu","sourceIds":["qul-56","qul-92","qul-71","qul-75","qul-76","qul-301"]}]}